{"type": "thinking", "text": "The criteria dropdown shows:\n- New cards only\n- Due cards only\n- All review cards in random order\n- All cards in random order (don't reschedule)\n\nIn AnkiDroid's deck options for filtered decks, the \"cards state\" selector should list criteria based on scheduler. In recent AnkiDroid, when using the new backend scheduler, the options include:\n- New cards only\n- Due cards only\n- All review cards in random order\n- All cards in random order (don't reschedule)\n- Preview new cards? Hmm.\n\nActually, in AnkiDroid the \"Study by card state or tag\" dialog offers these options. The changed build says \"the criteria dropdown now lists every selection criterion the scheduler offers.\" So maybe a criterion is missing. Let me think of what AnkiDroid's FilteredDeckOptions offers. In AnkiDroid source, CustomStudyDialog has options: STUDY_BY_CARD_STATE, STUDY_BY_TAG. Then StudyByCardStateDialog has a spinner with entries from R.array.study_by_card_state_dialog_labels? Let me recall.\n\nAnkiDroid strings:\n- \"New cards only\" = new cards\n- \"Due cards only\" = due cards\n- \"All review cards in random order\"\n- \"All cards in random order (don't reschedule)\"\n\nHmm, but \"every selection criterion the scheduler offers\" — hmm, there might be \"Preview new cards\" (which is a custom study option). Actually new filtered deck custom study has the 4 options. There's also \"All review cards in random order\" and \"All cards in random order\". In current AnkiDroid, StudyByCardStateDialog offers `new_card`, `due_card`, `review_card`, `all_card`. That's 4. Maybe there's a fifth one \"Preview new cards\"? No, that's separate.\n\nWait, maybe this is a different screen: In the deck options for a filtered deck, the \"Cards to include\" criteria dropdown (which is the filtered deck options screen) lists: New cards only, Due cards only, All review cards in random order, All cards in random order (don't reschedule). Also there might be \"Preview new cards\" but no.\n\nHmm, the changed area says \"Filtered deck builder: the criteria dropdown now lists every selection criterion the scheduler offers.\" This implies the fix adds missing criteria. So maybe the bug is the reverse: one criterion is now missing in this build? That seems odd. Changed in this build describes a change that may have introduced a bug. So maybe the dropdown now lists options but one of them is wrong/mislabeled, or duplicates.\n\nLet me consider Anki's built-in filtered deck criterion options in newer scheduler: In Anki desktop's filtered deck \"Search\" section there are predefined searches? No.\n\nActually, in AnkiDroid source (StudyByCardStateDialog.kt), the labels array is:\n- R.string.study_by_card_state_dialog_label_new_cards_only\n- R.string.study_by_card_state_dialog_label_due_cards_only\n- R.string.study_by_card_state_dialog_label_all_review_cards_random\n- R.string.study_by_card_state_dialog_label_all_cards_random\n\nThere might be added a 5th: \"Preview new cards\"? Hmm no.\n\nLet me check actual AnkiDroid versions. In CustomStudyDialog, options list historically:\n1. Increase today's new card limit\n2. Increase today's review card limit\n3. Review forgotten cards\n4. Review ahead\n5. Preview new cards\n6. Study by card state or tag\n\nThat matches exactly the 6 shown. So the custom study dialog is complete.\n\nNow the criteria dropdown showing 4 options. In the newer \"Study by card state or tag\" dialog, this appears to be a modern Compose-ish dialog. Possibly the scheduler offers 5 criteria including \"All cards in random order (don't reschedule)\" and something like \"New cards only\", \"Due cards only\", \"All review cards in random order\". Hmm.\n\nMaybe the missing criterion is \"Preview new cards\"? No.\n\nWait — in the Anki Desktop filtered deck options (deck options -> filtered deck), \"Cards to include\" search presets? Hmm.\n\nAlternatively this dialog might relate to \"study by card state\" where the criteria are the deck