{"type": "thinking", "text": "This is the filtered deck options screen. It has filter search \"deck:Spanish\", limit 4, \"Cards selected by\" spinner \"Random\", reschedule switch (off; because \"don't reschedule\"), delays. Good.\n\nNote: the criteria dropdown in the builder corresponds to filter search terms: \"deck:Spanish\" for all cards random; if \"New cards only\" it'd be \"deck:Spanish is:new\". Fine.\n\nNow, hold on: the spawn filter \"Cards selected by\" has options \"Random\", \"Due\", \"Added\", \"Order due\", etc. Not relevant.\n\nLet me test: Rebuild button. The deck has 4 cards. Press Rebuild -> should retain. But nothing to compare.\n\nNow back to criteria completeness. Let me inspect the source knowledge via app? Can't. But maybe there's a \"Help\" that documents. Hmm.\n\nI could check \"Preview new cards\" custom study: separate.\n\nLet me set the filtered deck's filter search to something and see error. Not needed.\n\nAlternative interpretation: \"Filtered deck builder: the criteria dropdown now lists every selection criterion the scheduler offers.\" Perhaps refers to the spinner in the \"Study by card state or tag\" dialog, where now one more criterion was added (maybe \"Preview new cards\"). Hmm wait, maybe the scheduler offers these five: \"New cards only\", \"Due cards only\", \"All review cards in random order\", \"All cards in random order (don't reschedule)\", and \"All cards in random order (reschedule)\"? Hmm, no.\n\nLet me think about AnkiDroid releases. The strings in AnkiDroid for custom study:\n\n```\n<string name=\"custom_study_new_cards_only\">New cards only</string>\n<string name=\"custom_study_due_cards_only\">Due cards only</string>\n<string name=\"custom_study_all_review_cards\">All review cards in random order</string>\n<string name=\"custom_study_all_cards_random\">All cards in random order (don\\'t reschedule)</string>\n```\n\nI'm fairly confident there are 4. Hmm, but what about \"Review cards only\" vs \"All review cards in random order\"? Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the scheduler also offers \"Learning cards only\"? Anki's custom study only offers \"new\", \"due\", \"review\", \"all\". So 4 = complete.\n\nMaybe the seeded bug is instead that one of the criteria is present but broken—e.g., choosing \"Due cards only\" actually uses the \"all cards\" search. Let's test each option's filter string via the filtered deck options screen (filter search input shows the search). That's a great way to verify: create a deck with each criterion and check the filter search.\n\nI'll test \"New cards only\" -> filter should be \"deck:Spanish is:new\". Let me do that later. But the current filtered deck is \"don't reschedule\" with search \"deck:Spanish\". \n\nActually, we can directly test criteria by creating custom study decks repeatedly and checking filter. But that creates multiple filtered decks (data changes). We can delete them after. Let's do: For each criterion, create a new filtered deck with count 100 from Spanish, then long-press -> Deck options -> read filter search string; delete deck. That's 4 decks. Reasonable.\n\nBut before heavy testing, address the likely seeded bug: maybe the dropdown lacks an option. Without knowing expected, functional tests might reveal mismatch: e.g., \"Due cards only\" search uses \"deck:Spanish is:due\" — correct. \"All review cards in random order\" -> \"deck:Spanish is:review\". \"New cards only\" -> \"deck:Spanish is:new\". \"All cards\" -> \"deck:Spanish\". If one is wrong, that's a bug.\n\nLet me close deck options (back twice?) and delete current filtered deck after tests. Actually I might keep it to test card counts.\n\nLet me first go test add note, then deck options (primary area), then come back to filtered criteria later.\n\nActually, let's do deck options now since we're near. Navigate back to deck list, long-press Spanish -> Deck options.\n\nPress back."}
