{"type": "thinking", "text": "Filter search is \"is:new deck:Spanish tag:verb\" correct. \"Cards selected by\" Order added. Good.\n\nNote: limit input still 4 though only 1 card. Fine.\n\nNow test each criterion mapping. But since the \"Study by card state or tag\" dialog's dropdown is the criteria builder, and we can see the resulting filter string via deck options. Let's test \"Due cards only\" and \"All review cards in random order\" and \"New cards only\" (done). Deleting current deck first.\n\nActually more efficient: edit the *existing* filtered deck's filter search? That doesn't test builder. Hmm.\n\nMaybe we can use Rebuild after changing filter? Not builder.\n\nPlan: delete current deck. Create filtered deck with each state and inspect filter strings. 3 more decks. Then delete.\n\nBut before that, what bug might exist in criteria? If the mapping is correct, then maybe no bug there. Also need test \"All cards in random order (don't reschedule)\" sets reschedule off (observed earlier: switch off, search \"deck:Spanish\"). Good.\n\nPotential bug: \"All review cards in random order\" filter \"deck:Spanish is:review\" but since no review cards, deck is empty; with allow-empty off, the deck may not be created at all (snackbar error \"No cards matched\"). That's expected. Hmm.\n\nLet me test \"Due cards only\" on French deck (3 new cards). Due cards only excludes new; French has no due cards -> likely empty deck creation error. Hmm, that won't give us a deck to inspect. Instead use count? No.\n\nAlternative: create in Spanish after introducing some review cards? Too much.\n\nHmm, maybe create with \"New cards only\" 4 -> deck \"is:new deck:Spanish\" (confirmed via tag test). \n\nTest \"Due cards only\" from French might create empty deck? Actually \"Create/update this deck even if empty\" default off, so if empty, creation fails with message like \"No cards matched\". That itself is expected Anki behavior. So can't inspect filter. But we could turn on allow-empty? Not in builder.\n\nActually maybe custom study dialog with \"Due cards only\" and no due cards still creates a deck? Let's test later.\n\nAlternatively, review a card in French to create a due/review card. That changes scheduling data but is within testing.\n\nHmm wait. Maybe the \"criteria dropdown\" bug is not mapping. Let me re-read the change: \"Filtered deck builder: the criteria dropdown now lists every selection criterion the scheduler offers.\" The \"criteria dropdown\" could be the dropdown in the *filtered deck options* \"Cards selected by\" spinner? No, that's sorting.\n\nWait, maybe the \"filtered deck builder\" is a separate screen reached from the deck picker's \"Create filtered deck\" menu item, which I noticed is missing from More options. Maybe the builder screen (like Anki desktop's \"Create Filtered Deck\" dialog) has name, search, limit, order, reschedule. Hmm, AnkiDroid doesn't have a create filtered deck dialog? Actually AnkiDroid 2.16 does have \"Create filtered deck\" in deck picker overflow. It opens a dialog with \"Deck name\", \"Search\", \"Limit\", \"Cards selected by\", \"Reschedule\", \"Create/update even if empty\". That is exactly the same screen as deck options filtered (with Rebuild). Hmm, but our overflow menu lacks \"Create filtered deck\"! That's suspicious.\n\nLet me check the More options menu again carefully. It had 6 items: Check, Create backup, Restore from backup, Manage note types, Import, Export. AnkiDroid 2.16 deck picker overflow also has \"Create filtered deck\" probably. If missing, that's a navigation bug in filtered decks area but unrelated to dropdown.\n\nHmm, maybe \"Create filtered deck\" is hidden because the build is configured with `newReviewer`? No.\n\nBut wait, this task's areas: \"filtered decks\" - the builder. The changed note says criteria dropdown. Maybe the \"Create filtered deck\" builder screen is reachable via deck options of filtered deck (Rebuild) only. Hmm.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: The dialog \"Study by card state or tag\" we used is our filtered deck builder. It has the criteria dropdown. Fine.\n\nWhat selection criteria does the scheduler offer? Maybe this dropdown previously only listed \"New cards only\" and \"Due cards only\" and \"All review cards...\" but \"All cards...\" was added. We see all 4. So no missing.\n\nUnless... the dropdown should also include \"All cards in random order (reschedule)\"? Hmm, no, reschedule is a separate switch.\n\nHmm, maybe the fifth criterion is \"Preview new cards\"? Let me check Anki Desktop quickly from memory: In Anki's custom study, \"Study by card state or tag\" dialog has radio buttons:\n- New cards only\n- Due cards only\n- All review cards in random order\n- All cards in random order (don't reschedule)\nAnd a tag field: \"Select tags\" optional. So 4.\n\nI think the dropdown is complete. Maybe the bug is the truncated last option (\"All cards in random order (don't res..\"). The build \"lists every selection criterion\" but the popup width cuts the last label. Hmm, that's a cut_off symptom. I could report it. But would the developer accept? The observed quote \"All cards in random order (don't res..\" appears on screen, element 39 earlier. It's genuinely truncated. But is that a bug? In Material dropdown, the popup width can be wider than the anchor. Other labels fit. A long label truncates. It's a minor visual defect but real: user can't read the full criterion, particularly \"(don't reschedule)\" is important. The field shows full text after selection, though. Hmm.\n\nWait, actually the field text itself when selected showed full \"All cards in random order (don't reschedule)\" - and it may also be truncated in the field? In observe [20] text was full. In the screenshot of field (before selection) I didn't see. Let me check the field display after selecting that option — the earlier screenshot with dropdown open showed field text \"New cards only\".\n\nAnyway, let's keep this as a candidate but keep looking for more substantive bugs.\n\nLet me now test the filtered deck builder edge: count input values. Set count 0 or negative or > cards. Expected: count 0 maybe error \"must be positive\" or creates empty. Also non-numeric. And empty. Might reveal crash.\n\nAlso test: switch criterion after count etc.\n\nBut more important areas: adding/editing notes and add note dismissal. Let's move to that and return to filtered deck later.\n\nBefore leaving filtered deck: delete the current filtered deck to restore Spanish (3) → 4. Long-press deck -> Delete. Also note the deck options screen for filtered deck: check \"Enable second filter\" toggle, etc. Not needed.\n\nDelete filtered deck."}
