{"type": "thinking", "text": "Empty swap: exits without prompt (correct). So the bug is specifically: typed content + model swap -> no discard prompt. Good.\n\nBut wait: maybe the snapshot \"rebuilt on each note model swap\" snapshots the new blank state of the new model, so any typed content in old model is compared against blank new model and should be detected as changed! Hmm, but \"prueba\" was carried over into the new model's Front field. So snapshot after swap = \"prueba\" baseline, and then no further changes => no prompt. Exactly.\n\nBut there's another scenario: type content, switch model, then edit more. Would it prompt? Snapshot rebuilt at swap includes old content; subsequent edits would differ -> prompt. So bug only after swap without further edits. Still a real bug: user types, changes type, navigates back → silently loses.\n\nAlso consider: type content, switch model, then change it back to Basic. The snapshot rebuild might be from current state each time. Still no prompt.\n\nNeed to file report. Screen: Add note screen. Element: the note type spinner (element 6 in latest Add observe, but latest observe is deck list). Need element_ref from latest observe at the time of report. The bug is about missing dialog, so element_ref should point at closest element - the note type spinner. Need to re-open Add note and switch model to have a latest observe with that element. But I can file with the element number from an observation; latest observe now is deck list. The instructions: element_ref from your latest observe. So I should re-create state, observe, then file. Let me do a clean reproduction and screenshot; then file.\n\nSteps:\n1. Open Add (FAB, Add).\n2. Type \"qa1\" in Front.\n3. Switch note type to Basic (and reversed card).\n4. Press back.\n5. Observe deck list (screen changed) → file report observing that it dismissed without prompt.\n\nBut observed_quote: The defect is a missing prompt, so quote can be omitted. But the instruction says \"a report