think element_ref validation might check that the element existed in the last observation before the report. Since the report is about missing prompt, maybe they just need an element that exists. Safer: perform the repro so the final screen is Add screen? But the bug only manifests on dismissal (decks list). Hmm.\n\nActually maybe I can demonstrate a related manifestation on the Add screen: after switching model, the screen doesn't track edits. There's no visual indicator though.\n\nAnother thought: maybe the same bug manifests when tapping the \"up\" arrow (navigate up) after model swap. Same thing.\n\nI'll do: reopen Add, type, switch model, observe (spinner + content), then tap navigate up (element 0) instead of back, observe deck list, then file with element_ref of spinner (6) and no quote or quote \"prueba\". Hmm.\n\nLet me first also test other add/edit note behaviors before filing, to batch reports:\n- Adding a note normally: does it save correctly and appear in deck/browser? Need to verify note creation works (no bug). We shouldn't leave test notes; could undo? We can add then delete via browser. Or use \"prueba\" note and then delete.\n- Editing an existing note: open note from browser, change field, save, verify persistence; test back without save -> discard prompt; rotation during edit.\n- The \"Add note\" screen with model swap + Save: does it save with the new model and correct cards? Test.\n- Add note: deck selection persists? etc.\n\nAlso the add note screen might have another seeded bug related to snapshot: after switching model and typing, then saving, reopening and... eh.\n\nLet me test \"Add note normally\" after this. I'll add a note to Spanish deck with front \"QA test\" back \"QA\", then verify in browser, then delete it.\n\nBut careful: data changes minimal; acceptable if cleaned up.\n\nLet me re-open Add and do the repro for the report first.\n\nActually, before filing, let me also examine if the discard prompt appears using the \"navigate up\" arrow after model swap (same no-prompt). One repro enough. Let's do clean repro with screenshot maybe. The screenshot will show Add screen with typed content and swapped type, not the missing prompt. Not useful. The missing-prompt event can't be screenshot after the fact.\n\nI'll file the report after re-observing Add screen with the state, then press back and confirm. Actually the file_report call returns developer reply; I can call it after confirming silently dismissed. Let me do:\n\n1. Open Add, type \"qa-dismiss\", switch to Basic (and reversed card), observe → note element numbers & quote.\n2. Press back → deck list (confirm no prompt).\n3. File report using element_ref from step 1's observation (spinner). observed_quote = \"qa-dismiss\" maybe (the typed content that was lost). Hmm, quote must show defect; the lost content is \"qa-dismiss\" and model \"Basic (and reversed card)\". The defect is the missing prompt. I can quote the typed text that was discarded. Probably fine.\n\nLet's do it."}
