al data-less steps. Fine.\n\nActually, I already have the reproduction. To be safe for element_ref, let me reopen Add and reproduce up to the pre-dismissal state, observe, then file. Then after file, press back to demonstrate again? Not needed.\n\nLet me do that but I also want to continue testing Add note save/edit. I'll combine: create a real note now.\n\nPlan for Add tests:\nA) Add note normal: open Add, choose Spanish deck, type Front \"prueba QA\", Back \"respuesta\", Tags \"verb\"? Then Save. Check snackbar and counts (Spanish 4->5?) Wait, Spanish has 4 new; adding one makes 5. Then browser check note exists with tags. Then delete it to clean up (via browser long-press -> delete note). Deleting card changes data again; but fine, restore 4.\n\nBut do I need to add a note? Testing \"adding notes\" area includes verifying save persists. Yes.\n\nB) Edit note: open \"comer\" in browser, edit field, save, verify. Then revert. Need deck counts unaffected.\n\nC) Add note dismissal bug (already found). Also check: type content, switch model, then tap Save -> does it save as the new model? Could be fine.\n\nAlso check rotation: on Add screen with content, rotate -> content retained; then back -> prompt? If snapshot bug also affects rotation, maybe content lost on rotation! That's important: rotate recreates activity; if edit tracking snapshot is bad, maybe unsaved content lost? Let's test: type content, rotate, see if content remains. That's a common bug. I'll test.\n\nD) The \"keep editing\" reversal works (tested).\n\nLet's do A now. Open Add."}
