min(preset, today)=1. If override → 1. Ambiguous.\n\nAt step 4: preset 2, today 20 → effective 2. min → 2; override → 20→4. So effective uses min. At step 5: custom study +2 → effective 4 (> preset 2), so custom study sets today's limit to 22? Then min(2,22)=2, not 4. So not min. Unless custom study increase also raises preset? No, preset stayed 2 (reopen showed 2). Hmm. So custom study increase sets something that *overrides* preset (not min), while deck options Today-only 20 doesn't override preset.\n\nThis strongly suggests the deck options \"Today only\" isn't being applied at all (or is stored somewhere else and ignored). Hmm, but step 1: today-only 1 with preset 25 gave 1, which contradicts \"ignored\" (would be 4). Unless preset at that time was 1? Wait! What if editing Today-only actually writes to the *preset* (bug from changed build: \"daily limits are now stored on the deck's options preset\")?\n\nLet's re-examine: At step 1, I opened Spanish options (Preset tab presumably selected, value 25), tapped Today only tab, set 1, saved. If the save wrote 1 to the preset (ignoring scope), preset would become 1. Then deck count 1. Reopen: Preset tab would show 1, Today tab maybe 1. But later we saw preset 25 again after reset, so not.\n\nHmm, at step 3 reset today-only to 20 and saved. Then step 4 set Preset to 2 and saved. If today-only 20 truly applied as override, effective 20 → 4. Observed 2. So today-only not applied. But at step 1 today-only 1 gave 1... Maybe because preset then was 1? No, preset was 25.\n\nUnless the deck list count at step 1 (Spanish 1) was because... Spanish had 4 cards and today-only=1 applied; yes.\n\nHmm, wait, maybe I mis-sequenced: Before step 1, did I set preset to 25? Yes. Let me recheck: after French This-deck 30, I reopened French: preset 25, this-deck 30. Then later on Spanish options, preset 25. Then Today only 1 → save → deck list Spanish 1. So yes, today-only=1 applied.\n\nThen reset to 20 (via reset) → save → deck list 4. That's expected with 20 (all 4 available). Then preset 2 → save → deck list 2, even though today-only should still be 20 (unless the preset save reset today's limit to the new preset, i.e., 2). If the preset save overwrote today's limit with the preset value (2), then effective 2. That would be a bug: changing preset daily limit resets today-only limit. Hmm! Is that the seeded bug? \"daily limits are now stored on the deck's options preset\" — perhaps the bug is that setting the preset daily limit also resets the today-only limit (because they share storage)? Hmm.\n\nBut wait, after preset save to 2, reopening Today-only showed 20 still, not 2. So if the preset save overwrote today's limit, the Today tab would show 2. It showed 20. So no.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the *displayed* Today-only 20 is stale in UI only, and backend today limit was actually reset by preset save. The backend value would be 2 after preset save; UI still displays 20 from some cached \"preset\" value? Hmm.\n\nThen custom study +2 sets backend today limit = preset 2 + 2 = 4 (correct). UI still displays 20 (stale). That is consistent! Maybe the deck options Today-only field is just displaying the wrong value (always shows 20/default or stale). Let's test: after the custom study +2 (today limit presumably 4), reopen Today-only shows 20. If I now type 1 in Today-only and save, effective should become 1 if the field works. Deck list Spanish would show 1. Let's test that; if it works, then the field is functional. Then restore with custom study? Hmm.\n\nActually, we already did a similar test at step 1: typed 1 → effective 1. So field works. So the issue is that the *displayed* 20 in Today-only after preset change is not what's in effect: actual today limit may have been 2 (from preset), while UI still shows 20? Wait, but in step 4 the UI showed 20 after preset save; actual effective 2. If I had pressed Save without changing, would it write 20? Maybe yes, which would restore 20 override. Hmm, we didn't save in step 5. So UI displayed 20 but actual today limit was 2 (preset fallback). This suggests the UI's Today-only tab displays a stale/cached value rather than the actual today limit.\n\nHmm, wait: Maybe there is no actual today-only limit set; the display of \"20\" under Today-only is showing the *default* value (20) as a placeholder, not an actual override. Like, when no override is set, the field shows the default 20 in gray? But in screenshot, the value 20 looked black. Hmm, in AnkiDroid deck options, when there's no override, the field might display the preset's value in a lighter color? Actually in the screenshot after reset, the Today-only tab was blue and value 20 black.\n\nHmm, let me look at the earlier screenshot: The \"Today only\" field showed \"20\" black. If placeholder it'd be gray.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the reset button (\"Restore this setting to its default value?\") sets TODAY's limit to 20 (the Anki default), and Save stores it, but the value is reset to the preset's value (2?) at... no.\n\nLet me do a decisive experiment:\nCurrent state: preset 2; effective today limit = 4 (after custom study +2 → today 4); Today-only UI shows 20.\nExperiment A: Change Today-only to 1, save. Check deck list: if 1 → today-only field works.\nExperiment B: After that, change preset to e.g. 10, save. Check Today-only tab value and deck list. If deck list becomes 4 (cards) while today-only UI still 1, then preset save resets today's limit/ignores it. Hmm.\n\nThen restore: to return to clean state (preset 20, no overrides). We can use reset buttons maybe, or set preset 20 and today 20, this deck 20, which is effectively default. That's fine.\n\nActually, the changed-build bug might be exactly that: editing the preset's daily limit resets/overrides the \"Today only\" limit (or \"This deck\" limit) because limits are now stored on the preset. Let's test B carefully.\n\nBut before more, maybe I should consider what the hidden bug likelihood is. The task's three areas likely each contain one seeded bug; we found one in add note. The other two likely have bugs. Our deck-options testing so far hasn't revealed a clear-cut bug except this Today-only inconsistency. The filtered deck criteria dropdown seems complete (4 options). Hm", "truncated": true}
