concrete and verifiable, with screen quotes. But I need to be sure of expected behavior: In Anki, today-only limit should override preset. I'm fairly confident. Also our earlier observation of today-only=1 with preset=25 showing 1 demonstrates the intended behavior. So this is a regression triggered by changing the preset? That's a valid bug: after changing the preset's new cards/day, the Today-only limit stops being applied.\n\nBut wait, maybe the deck options save flow is: when you press Save, it saves the preset (new=20) AND saves all three tabs? The Today-only value 1 should then be applied. It isn't. So yes, bug.\n\nHowever, is this seeded-bug-related? The changed item: \"Deck options New cards section: the daily limits are now stored on the deck's options preset.\" Hmm, maybe the intended bug is precisely that setting the preset's new limit overwrites the per-deck/today limit. Plausible!\n\nBut before reporting, let me test a cleaner sequence to isolate:\n1. Set Today only = 1 (with preset 20), Save → deck list should show 1.\n2. Then open options, change Preset to 5, Save → deck list: if it shows 4 (today 1 ignored → preset 5? shows 4 since only 4 available) then bug. If shows 1, then preset change doesn't break today.\nLet's do this. Currently preset 20, today 1 (displayed, not effective). Step 1: open options, Today-only tab (probably selected), set 1 (already 1) and Save without changes? That may not save if unchanged. Hmm. Better set Today-only 2, Save → verify Spanish 2. Then open options, set Preset 5, Save → verify Spanish. If Spanish becomes 4 → today 2 ignored; if 2 → today honored.\n\nLet's do it. Currently in reviewer. Back."}
