Ugh, cycles.\n\nActually, hmm: maybe the deck options Today-only settings are applied only when the value is *lower* than the preset? That's \"min\" semantics. With preset 20, today 2 → min=2 → should 2, but observed 4. So no.\n\nWait, maybe I misread the deck list count: \"Spanish | 4 | 0 | 0\" means 4 new. If today-only=2 applied, it'd be 2. So no.\n\nCould it be that the save didn't happen because the \"Save\" button was not the right one (maybe [21] was \"Save\" text but the actual button [3] was Save; in keyboard state, the Save button is [21] yes). It did navigate back, so save happened.\n\nCould the Today-only change require the field to lose focus before Save? We typed and immediately tapped Save; the tap should commit text. Earlier it worked.\n\nWait, maybe the Today-only value saves but is **not used because the preset value is now 20 and today-only 2 should be a *cap* on top of preset when preset < available**... no.\n\nLet me check the \"Increase today's new card limit\" behavior again from the current polluted state: available new cards 4. The dialog earlier said \"Available new cards: 4\". It increased to 4. So after that, today's limit is 4. Then deck options Today-only shows values 1/2 but actual limit remains 4 (custom study). So deck options Today-only edits are ignored because custom-study today limit 4 is stored separately and takes precedence! That explains everything after the custom study increase. Before that, deck options Today-only worked.\n\nHmm, but after custom study increase, effective limit 4. We then set Today-only=1 and got 3 (not 4). That contradicts (if custom-study 4 persisted, should 4). Unless setting deck options Today-only=1 *did* apply partially... ugh.\n\nActually wait: maybe the \"Increase today's new card limit by 2\" created a **filtered deck**? No.\n\nHmm, maybe the deck list \"3\" was because the custom study today limit was 4 and deck options Today-only 1 set... I don't know.\n\nI need to stop and reassess strategy. I've spent a lot of steps. There are 3 areas; I found one clear bug. I should examine the filtered deck area more carefully for a clear bug, then decide whether the deck options area has a clear bug.\n\nLet me consider the possibility that the deck options seeded bug is simpler and visible: \"Daily limits are now stored on the deck's options preset.\" Maybe the bug is that **the \"This deck\" and \"Today only\" tabs are non-functional** (they write to the preset or are ignored). But our results are inconsistent. Or maybe the seeded bug is that the default New cards/day **is 20 but displayed as 20** — no.\n\nHold on, reconsider the very first preset test: I changed New cards/day on the \"Preset\" tab from 20 to 25 and saved. Reopened French and it showed 25 (preset). Good. Maybe the bug: **the preset's daily limits are stored but not applied to the deck counts until app restart**? No, counts changed with preset 2 (Spanish 2).\n\nAlternatively, maybe the bug is that the **\"Maximum reviews/day\" preset edit does not persist**. Let's test that cleanly: currently preset new=20, today=2 (ineffective). Set Maximum reviews/day Preset = 150, save, reopen, check 150 in Spanish and French. If it doesn't persist, that's a clear bug. Let's do it.\n\nOpen options."}
