{"type": "thinking", "text": "Data mostly restored: preset new/day 20, reviews 200, French this-deck 20, Spanish today-only 2 (ineffective/stale, harmless? maybe). Hmm.\n\nNow, let me spend remaining effort on the filtered deck area, because that's likely where a clear bug lies. Let's look at the \"Create filtered deck\" builder screen. The changed note: \"criteria dropdown now lists every selection criterion the scheduler offers.\" Maybe \"criteria dropdown\" refers to the **\"Cards selected by\"** spinner (sort order). We saw 11 options. Perhaps the scheduler offers 12 including \"Oldest seen first\" and \"Random\"... Hmm, Anki's sort order enum in newer versions might include \"Order added\" and \"Latest added first\" etc. 11 is what AnkiDroid has. But maybe one is missing: \"Relative overdueness\"? present. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the dropdown is the deck options \"Filter\" search with a dropdown of *filter criteria*? Hmm no.\n\nWait! The tag selection dialog had a \"Filter tags\" button [1]. Maybe tapping it shows a criteria dropdown? no.\n\nWhat about the **\"Search\" button** in the builder (magnifier) opening the card browser search with \"Sort Field\", \"Card Type\", \"Due\", \"Deck\" header buttons? Hmm no.\n\nLet me think about the phrase again: \"Filtered deck builder: the criteria dropdown now lists every selection criterion the scheduler offers.\" A \"selection criterion\" in the filtered deck builder = the options in the \"Select x cards...\" dialog dropdown: New cards only, Due cards only, All review cards in random order, All cards in random order (don't reschedule). The scheduler offers 4 selection criteria. They are all listed → no bug. Unless... the scheduler offers a **fifth**: \"Review cards in order added\"? Hmm no.\n\nWait — maybe the new scheduler supports \"All cards in random order (reschedule)\" as separate from don't-reschedule? Hmm, the switch handles reschedule.\n\nAlternatively, AnkiDroid's actual dialog might have 5 options historically:\n1. New cards only\n2. Due cards only\n3. All review cards in random order\n4. All cards in random order (don't reschedule)\n5. All cards in random order (reschedule)? No.\n\nHmm, actually! I recall AnkiDroid's `StudyByCardStateDialog` has options based on `CustomStudy` options:\n- `NEW_CARDS_ONLY`\n- `DUE_CARDS_ONLY`\n- `REVIEW_CARDS`\n- `ALL_CARDS`\nThat's 4.\n\nCould the \"criteria dropdown\" be the **\"Cards selected by\"** sort dropdown, and the scheduler offers **12 sort orders** in this build? The 11 we saw might be missing \"Order added\"?? It's there. Let me enumerate Anki's `SortOrder` from Anki's proto (anki_pb2):\nSORT_TYPE_OLDEST_SEEN_FIRST = 0\nSORT_TYPE_RANDOM = 1\nSORT_TYPE_INTERVAL_ASCENDING = 2\nSORT_TYPE_INTERVAL_DESCENDING = 3\nSORT_TYPE_LAPSES = 4\nSORT_TYPE_ADDED_ORDER = 5\nSORT_TYPE_DUE_ORDER = 6\nSORT_TYPE_ADDED_ORDER_DESC = 7\nSORT_TYPE_RETRIEVABILITY_ASCENDING = 8\nSORT_TYPE_RETRIEVABILITY_DESCENDING = 9\nSORT_TYPE_RELATIVE_OVERDUENESS = 10\nThat's 11. Yes exactly. So complete.\n\nHmm, maybe the filtered-deck bug is not about the dropdown content but behavior: e.g., in the builder, changing the criteria dropdown (sort) doesn't persist after Build? Or the filter limits? Let's test the FAB \"Create filtered deck\" flow:\n- It defaulted filter \"deck:French is:due\", limit 100, sort Random, reschedule ON, allow empty OFF.\n- Build button. If no cards match (French has no due), what happens? It may create empty deck? With allow-empty off, should show error. Test input boundary: Build with no matching cards → error message? Could reveal bug.\n- Create a valid filtered deck: filter \"deck:Spanish\", limit 4, sort \"Order added\", reschedule toggle, Build → deck created with 4 cards. Check filter/search persists, sort persists. Delete.\n\nAlso test \"Build\" with invalid search syntax e.g. \"is:new deck:\" → error. Not in changed area though.\n\nAlso test \"Rebuild\" existing deck after changing sort. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the seeded bug: When creating a filtered deck via the FAB, the \"Cards selected by\" sort dropdown's selected value is not saved (e.g., always Random). We can test: create with \"Order added\", build, open deck options, check spinner shows \"Order added\". If it shows Random, bug.\n\nAlso test the \"Enable second filter\" switch: add second filter with criteria; bug possible. Hmm.\n\nLet's do these functional tests now.\n\nFirst, create a filtered deck from FAB with Spanish, \"New cards only\" maybe via search field \"deck:Spanish is:new\", limit 4, sort \"Order added\", reschedule off, allow empty off. Then Build. Check deck created with 4 new cards, and deck options show \"deck:Spanish is:new\", limit 4, sort Order added, reschedule off. Then delete.\n\nBut wait, deck builder default filter is \"deck:French is:due\"; if we type Spanish etc. Let's use FAB. From deck list, tap Add FAB → Create filtered deck."}
