ts every selection criterion\" — a truncated label still lists it. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe there were **two** identical options because the scheduler has 5 including an alias? Not.\n\nCould the criteria dropdown be missing **\"Learning cards only\"**? Hmm, Anki's scheduler supports `is:learn`, and the custom study \"Study by card state or tag\" in newer Anki (2.1.60) might offer:\n- New cards only\n- Due cards only\n- All review cards in random order\n- All cards in random order (don't reschedule)\nHmm, no learn.\n\nWhat about \"Review ahead\" and \"Preview new cards\"? They're separate menu items and produce filtered decks with specific criteria, not dropdown options. So dropdown complete.\n\nMaybe the seeded bug in filtered decks is instead in the **tag selection**: \"No other tags exist\" — the tag dialog showed only \"verb\", correct. Hmm.\n\nOr in the **custom study count**: \"Select x cards from the deck:\" with count 100; if you enter more than available, the deck gets capped (4). Fine.\n\nOr the **\"Increase today's new card limit\"** dialog: \"Available new cards: 4\" was correct at that time. Fine.\n\nHmm. Let me look at the deck list after creating a filtered deck: the filtered deck count shows \"0 | 0 | 4\" with reschedule off; and Spanish \"0\". Header \"7 cards due\". When we deleted, cards returned. Fine.\n\nWhat about the filtered deck study: after studying a card from a \"don't reschedule\" deck, does it return to the original deck? Hard but maybe.\n\nAlternatively, maybe \"Rebuild\" is broken: after changing the filter/limit in filtered deck options and pressing Rebuild, the deck should be rebuilt with new settings/count. Test: create filtered deck 4 cards; change limit to 1; Rebuild; deck should show 1 card and return 3 to Spanish. Let's test; if Rebuild doesn't apply limit, bug. This is in filtered decks area but not the changed note. Still valid QA sweep.\n\nLet's do that: create filtered deck (New cards only, Spanish, 2). Then options change limit to 1 + Rebuild. Check deck counts. We have few steps; maybe prioritize.\n\nActually, hold on. Maybe I should reconsider the changed note #2: \"the criteria dropdown now lists every selection criterion the scheduler offers.\" Could refer to the **deck options \"New cards/day\"**? no. Could refer to the **filtered deck options \"Cards selected by\"** — \"selection criterion\" might be the sort criterion, and \"the scheduler offers\" refers to the scheduling order. Hmm. If the drop-down was updated to list all sort orders, maybe the bug is that the 11th option \"Relative overdueness\" (or \"Descending retrievability\") is present but selecting it crashes or doesn't persist. We could test the last option \"Relative overdueness\" persistence in a filtered deck. Hmm.\n\nLet me test selecting each sort value? Too many. But test one non-default: \"Order added\" persisted (we saw). So mapping works.\n\nMaybe the seeded bug is that the builder's dropdown is missing **\"Relative overdueness\"**? No, it's there.\n\nHmm, let me look at the dropdown for the *study-by-card-state* again and inspect if any option is duplicated or text wrong. Options:\n1. New cards only\n2. Due cards only\n3. All review cards in random order\n4. All cards in random order (don't res.. [truncated]\n\nMaybe expected option 4 is \"All cards in random order (don't reschedule)\" and there should be a **5th: \"All cards in random order (reschedule)\"**? In AnkiDroid's `StudyByCardStateDialog`, when you pick \"All cards\", it might ask whether to reschedule? Actually, the custom study decks always reschedule by default; \"All cards in random order (don't reschedule)\" is the only non-rescheduling option. So no.\n\nI think the only concrete filtered-deck defect might be the truncation. Let me verify the field displays the full text after selection, and whether the popup truncation is due to narrow width. Maybe the menu item itself is clipped by the popup's width, but a long-press or scroll could reveal? The popup width = 720 like the field. On a 1080-wide screen, the popup could be wider. This is a genuine visual bug but low severity. The task's symptom types include \"cut_off\", and the instruction says report cut off. The changed area is that dropdown. I lean toward reporting it as a minor bug, especially since the QA instructions emphasize cut_off.\n\nBut wait, the label in the dropdown reads \"All ca", "truncated": true}
