{"type": "text", "text": "The device connection has dropped permanently (`BrokenPipeError` on every `device` call, including `observe`, `open_app`, `press_key`, and `file_report`), so I can no longer operate the app or call `sign_off`. I will not sign off, because the sweep was not complete and there are unverified areas.\n\n## What I found and logged\n\n**Confirmed bug (logged by developer):**\n- **Add note — unsaved edit silently discarded after note-type swap**\n  - Add note → type `qa-dismiss` in Front → switch Type Basic → “Basic (and reversed card)” → press Back.\n  - Expected: “Discard current input?” prompt.\n  - Observed: Add screen closes straight to the deck list with no prompt; typed content lost. Without the model swap, the same edit correctly shows “Discard current input?” (Keep editing / Discard). Developer replied: *“thanks, confirmed and logged. Keep testing the current build.”*\n\n## Areas exercised (no clean bug found before the device died)\n\n- **Adding/editing notes:** adding a note to Spanish worked (note appeared in Browser, count 5→4 after deleting it); editing persisted; Discard/Keep editing on the edit screen worked; rotation preserved unsaved text; tags and the tag dialog showed only `verb` as expected.\n- **Filtered decks:** created filtered decks via both “Custom study → Study by card state or tag” and the FAB “Create filtered deck”; verified counts, tag filter (`verb` → comer only), filter search text, sort order persistence, reschedule switch, empty-search error (“No cards matched…”), and deletion returning cards to the original deck. Criteria dropdown showed all 4 options (New/Due/All review/All cards don’t-reschedule).\n- **Deck options:** New cards/day and Maximum reviews/day edits persisted on the “Default” preset and were visible from both Spanish and French; “This deck” override persisted; reset-to-default and save/discard worked.\n\n## Open/unresolved items (not filed, because not confirmed before the outage)\n\n- In the criteria dropdown popup, the last item renders ellipsized as **“All cards in random order (don't res..“** (full text appears once selected). Possible minor `cut_off`.\n- Deck options “Today only” new cards/day became inconsistent after preset/custom-study edits: the field showed a value (e.g. 2) while Spanish still showed 4 new due / reviewer New 4. I was in the middle of isolating this when the device died.\n- The final action — “Due cards only” + **Choose tags** — coincided with the device connection loss; I could not determine whether it was a device/infrastructure failure or an app crash.\n\n## Data state at the outage\n\nMostly restored: preset New cards/day 20, Maximum reviews/day 200, French “This deck” 20; Spanish “Today only” holds a leftover 2. One test side effect was **not** reset: French note **bonjour** was graded “Easy” (now a review card due in 4 days) while testing the “All review cards” criterion."}
